This provides a basic way to restrict access to certain pages or services to only logged-in users. The actual login process and session management would need to be implemented separately.

Note that this just handles the server-side access control. You'd also want to remove any links or UI elements that link to restricted pages for users who aren't logged in. But the script ensures even if someone tries to access the URL directly, they will be denied if not authenticated.

